From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:34:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/78] Do not turn non-strict float compare+assign into
 min/max without fastmath

MINSD/MAXSD return the second operand when both compare equal, so
'if x <= 0 then x := 0' keeps -0.0. No single MINSD/MAXSD ordering
matches the if-statement for both NaN and signed zero, so only allow
lten/gten on floats under cs_opt_fastmath.
---
 compiler/nflw.pas | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/nflw.pas b/compiler/nflw.pas
index 8e63b6d7..14bfe0db 100644
--- a/compiler/nflw.pas
+++ b/compiler/nflw.pas
@@ -1717,6 +1717,11 @@ implementation
           (thenstmnt.nodetype=assignn) and ((t1=nil) or (elsestmnt.nodetype=assignn)) and
           not(might_have_sideeffects(left)) and
           ((t1=nil) or tassignmentnode(thenstmnt).left.isequal(tassignmentnode(elsestmnt).left)) and
+          { MINSD/MAXSD return the second operand for +0/-0, so a non-strict
+            float comparison cannot be mapped to min/max without fastmath }
+          not((left.nodetype in [lten,gten]) and
+              (is_single(tassignmentnode(thenstmnt).left.resultdef) or is_double(tassignmentnode(thenstmnt).left.resultdef)) and
+              not(cs_opt_fastmath in current_settings.optimizerswitches)) and
 {$if defined(i386) or defined(x86_64)}
 {$ifdef i386}
           (((current_settings.fputype>=fpu_sse) and is_single(tassignmentnode(thenstmnt).left.resultdef)) or
